## 6. Result (final unified dataset)

**20,415 images · 106,651 objects · 10 classes**

| ID | Class | Objects | Share |
|----|-------|--------:|------:|
| 0 | car | 21,550 | 20.2% |
| 1 | bus_truck | 18,034 | 16.9% |
| 3 | cng | 18,116 | 17.0% |
| 2 | rickshaw | 15,043 | 14.1% |
| 7 | pedestrian | 10,581 | 9.9% |
| 4 | motorbike | 10,050 | 9.4% |
| 8 | paddlefoot_transportation | 5,847 | 5.5% |
| 5 | bicycle | 3,563 | 3.3% |
| 9 | auto_transportation | 2,486 | 2.3% |
| 6 | human_hauler | 1,381 | 1.3% |

- **Imbalance reduced from 1825x to 16x** — from untrainable to standard.
- Every class present in **both** train and valid splits (earlier rare-class
  validation gap resolved by ODS_New volume).
- ODS_New supplies ~85% of objects (backbone); datasets 1–2 enrich. The
  contribution is the demonstrated multi-source, multi-format reconciliation.

---

## 7. Known limitations (stated honestly)

- Minority classes `human_hauler` (1,381) and `auto_transportation` (2,486) will
  likely show lower per-class recall; to be reported transparently.
- A small number of source JPEGs are mildly corrupt (truncated segments); these
  are skipped at load time and do not affect training materially.
- Residual 16x imbalance remains; can be addressed via class weighting or
  augmentation if needed.
- Two custom groupings (paddlefoot_transportation, auto_transportation) bundle
  visually heterogeneous vehicles; named for project-specific convenience and
  defined explicitly here for reader clarity.

---

## 8. Reproducibility

- Random seed fixed (42) for all splits.
- Raw sources never modified; all transforms write to new folders, giving a full
  audit trail.
- Pipeline scripts: `06_build_unified_dataset.py` (build),
  `08_validate_labels.py` (validate), `09_fix_label_coords.py` (repair).

---

## 9. Detector training (Phase 4 — for context)

Fine-tuned **YOLOv8m** on the unified dataset: 300 epochs (early stopping
patience 50), imgsz 1280, batch 2, RTX 3060 12GB, best weights saved.
High input resolution chosen to aid detection of small/distant vehicles in
overhead foot-overbridge footage.